Audit: what "ported but unwired" actually means here — 2026-09-10

Video coverage showed five port_md modules at 0.00 %. Counting PRODUCTION
callers (excluding tests) separates two very different situations:

  module                regions  prod callers  what it really is
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  tx_gates                 127        0        DUPLICATE of live inline code
  mv_refine                175        0        blocked on OBMC/warped motion
  motion_mode              265        0        blocked on OBMC/warped motion
  ssim_hbd                 214        0        blocked on hbd MODE DECISION
  md_stages                285        0        alternative MD-stage driver

1. tx_gates -- WIRED, and it was duplication, not a gap.
   `leaf_funnel/tx_geom.rs::end_tx_depth{,_inter}` carried a byte-for-byte copy
   of the same bsize table. Two ports of one C function is a divergence waiting
   to happen, so the live path now calls
   `port_md::tx_gates::get_end_tx_depth` and keeps only the class CAP, which is
   the part `get_start_end_tx_depth` contributes. Byte-neutral by construction
   (identical tables) and by measurement: identity 1100/1100,
   regression_spotcheck 141/141, inter_byte 108/108, screen_palette 50/50,
   real_video 24/24.

   tx_gates additionally implements C's frame-OVERHANG pin (a block crossing the
   aligned frame is forced to depth 0, `:6711-6717`), which tx_geom never had.
   It is unreachable here because blocks tile the ALIGNED frame, so this changes
   nothing today -- but it is now present for when that stops holding.

2. ssim_hbd -- NOT a wiring gap. C branches the tune-SSIM MD distortion on
   `ctx->hbd_md`; the port calls the 8-bit arm unconditionally
   (`mds3.rs:3077`, on `cand.y_recon`, with `cand.y_recon10` sitting right
   above). The module's own doc names this. But `hbd_md` is hardcoded `false`/`0`
   at EVERY site in the port (inter_hdr_arm.rs:452, inter_search_arm.rs:434 and
   :602): there is no high-bit-depth mode-decision path at all. Mode decision
   always runs 8-bit and 10-bit is a post-pass. So ssim_hbd cannot be wired
   until hbd MD exists; wiring it now would be adding a branch nothing can take.

3/4. mv_refine + motion_mode -- blocked on a FEATURE, not wiring. Both serve
   WARPED_CAUSAL / OBMC_CAUSAL, and no such candidate is ever injected
   (inter_md_arm.rs asserts only SimpleTranslation reaches the predictor).
   `warped_motion_mode_allowed` exists as a tested predicate with no producer.
   Making these active means implementing OBMC and warped motion end to end --
   candidate injection, the refinement searches, the rate, and C parity for
   each -- not connecting a call.

5. md_stages -- an alternative COMPLETE port of the MDS0..MDS3 class loop that
   `leaf_funnel` already drives its own way. Switching drivers is a refactor of
   working, byte-identical code; the payoff is one implementation instead of
   two, and the risk is a behaviour change in the single hottest path in the
   encoder. Worth doing deliberately, not opportunistically.

WHY THE PORT IS STILL BYTE-IDENTICAL WITHOUT THEM. If C used OBMC, warped
motion or hbd MD in the configurations under test, the bytes would already
differ -- and they do not (1100/1100 stills, 108/108 inter). So C is not
selecting those tools in this envelope either. The gap they represent is
RD-in-a-wider-envelope, not correctness here.

HONEST SCOPE: "wire everything" reduces to two features -- high-bit-depth mode
decision, and OBMC + warped motion -- plus one deliberate driver refactor. Each
needs its own C-parity campaign. One of the five was genuinely just duplication
and is now closed.
